# COMMON MODEL – SmartCartPro

## 1. Single file
- Shared enums + AJAX envelope live in `Models/CommonModel.cs` only.
- Do not split into `CommonEnums.cs` / duplicate response files.
- Do not copy Persuite CRM bloat (CRMConstants, WhatsApp helpers, etc.).

## 2. Structure
```csharp
public class CommonModel
{
    public enum LicenseStatus { Active = 1, Suspended = 2, Expired = 3, Trial = 4 }
    // Add more shared enums here as values only — no mapping helper classes.
}

public class CommonResponseModel
{
    public int StatusCode { get; set; }
    public string Status { get; set; }
    public string Message { get; set; }
    public object? Data { get; set; }
    public List<string>? Errors { get; set; }
    public string Timestamp { get; set; }
    // Success / Failure factories OK — used by CommonHelpers + AppExceptionHandler.
}
```

## 3. Enums that hit TEXT DB columns
- View/Input may use **int** + enum (e.g. `CommonModel.LicenseStatus`).
- Entity/DB may remain TEXT (e.g. `active` / `suspended`). Map in the **repository** only.
- Do not add public `*StatusCodes` helper classes on CommonModel; no schema change unless asked.

## 4. Custom validation attributes
- Live under `CustomModelValidation/`, namespace `SmartCartPro.CustomModelValidation`.
- Use on In…View only (see model-naming §7).
